OL,3,GNEWSA999 calls about tumble dryers
OL,4,Aafter wildfire alert
OL,5,
OL,6,FA fire service says it has seen a
OL,7,F"sharp spike" in non-emergency 999
OL,8,Fcalls after the government's nationwide
OL,9,Fwildfire alert, including people asking
OL,10,Fwhether it is safe to use their tumble
OL,11,Fdryer.
OL,13,FDavid Lynch, area manager for
OL,14,FLincolnshire Fire and Rescue, said
OL,15,Finquiries had included concerns over
OL,16,Fbonfires or barbeques, vegetation
OL,17,Fgrowing near people's homes, and
OL,18,Fresidents spotting cigarette butts
OL,19,Foutside their homes.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,387,380,200,160,0,100
